{"id":"city-and-medicaid","title":"Paid by the City and by Medicaid","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"When Medicaid began paying an organization for a service, did the City keep paying it the same?","finding":"32 organizations the City pays also bill Medicaid under their own name ($614 million, 2018 to 2024). For 7 of them the Medicaid money is new or has tripled since 2021, from $0.0 million to $21.4 million in 2024, while City payments to the same 7 went from $30.0 million (fiscal 2022) to $46.7 million (fiscal 2026). Seneca Family of Agencies is not counted: only its own billing number is new, and the raw federal rows show Medicaid paid $40.1 million in 2021 for its services under another biller's number.","how":"Billing organizations were matched by name to City-paid nonprofits and vendors. Flagged: at least $500,000 from Medicaid in 2024, under $50,000 or less than a third of that in 2021, City payments in fiscal 2026 no lower than nine tenths of fiscal 2022, and under $50,000 paid in 2021 for services the organization gave that another organization billed (the raw rows name both the billing and the servicing provider).","limits":"A name match is not proof the two are one legal body, and one name can cover several clinics. California added Medi-Cal benefits in 2022 for meals, care management and housing help, and City contracts may already subtract what Medicaid pays or cover people Medicaid does not. Whether both paid for the same service to the same person can only be seen in the contract budgets and invoices, which this file does not hold. Small cells are withheld and 2024 is preliminary. The fiscal year of a City payment here is the Controller's: the year its files put the payment under, the same year the organization pages show. For a small part of the money the voucher was issued in an earlier fiscal year than that: $97.3 million of the $10.22 billion in the City's nonprofit spending file for the nonprofits profiled here, going by the matching lines of the payment file; for a further $152.7 million the payment file has no matching lines, or lines that mix payments and reversals, so it cannot be said.","columns":[{"k":"org","t":"Organization","type":"org"},{"k":"pattern","t":"Pattern","type":"text"},{"k":"medicaid2021","t":"Medicaid 2021","type":"usd"},{"k":"medicaid2024","t":"Medicaid 2024","type":"usd"},{"k":"medicaidAll","t":"Medicaid 2018–2024","type":"usd"},{"k":"cityFY2022","t":"City, fiscal 2022","type":"usd"},{"k":"cityFY2026","t":"City, fiscal 2026","type":"usd"},{"k":"cityAll","t":"City since fiscal 2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"service","t":"Main Medicaid service, 2023–24","type":"text"},{"k":"billedByOthers","t":"Medicaid paid for its services under another biller’s number, 2018–2024","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"org":"Institute On Aging","orgKey":"INSTITUTE ON AGING","pattern":"New Medicaid money since 2021","medicaid2021":0,"medicaid2024":9075035,"medicaidAll":22963233,"billedByOthers":0,"cityFY2022":9588919,"cityFY2026":8835480,"cityAll":79318648,"service":"community wrap-around services, per day (code H2022)","billsAs":"Institute on Aging"},{"org":"Cardea Health","orgKey":"CARDEA HEALTH","pattern":"New Medicaid money since 2021","medicaid2021":0,"medicaid2024":4023800,"medicaidAll":5848870,"billedByOthers":0,"cityFY2022":0,"cityFY2026":1190229,"cityAll":2806688,"service":"residential care, per day (code T2033)","billsAs":"Cardea Health"},{"org":"Homebridge Inc","orgKey":"HOMEBRIDGE","pattern":"New Medicaid money since 2021","medicaid2021":0,"medicaid2024":3076000,"medicaidAll":3085700,"billedByOthers":0,"cityFY2022":445582,"cityFY2026":512537,"cityAll":3304776,"service":"case management (California uses it for Enhanced Care Management) (code G9012)","billsAs":"Homebridge Inc"},{"org":"Project Open Hand","orgKey":"PROJECT OPEN HAND","pattern":"New Medicaid money since 2021","medicaid2021":0,"medicaid2024":2961337,"medicaidAll":4367527,"billedByOthers":0,"cityFY2022":5385337,"cityFY2026":6833064,"cityAll":47269810,